7d(ii). How much of the nugget could be temporal?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Mean within-well VARIANCE across years (UP, 3+ readings): 1.983 m2
  Fitted nugget, single-year target, same wells:            4.506 m2
  Temporal noise is therefore at most 44.0% of the nugget.

  Averaging over k readings cuts the temporal part to roughly 1/k of that,
  so the most averaging could remove is about 44.0% of the nugget --
  and in practice less, since most wells have fewer than 5 readings.
  The remaining majority of the nugget is genuine micro-scale spatial
  variation plus measurement error, which no amount of temporal averaging
  can touch.

